{{also|hub-bub}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|whobub}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Mid 16<sup>th</sup>c. Perhaps from {{bor|en|ga|-}}; compare Irish ''[[ababú]]!'', ''[[abú]]!'' (battle-cry), Gaelic ''[[ub|ub! ub!]]'' (expressing contempt, etc.), ''[[ubh ubh]]!'' (expressing disgust).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhʌbʌb/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hubbub.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[confuse]]d [[uproar]], [[commotion]], [[tumult]] or [[racket]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|2|passage=At length a universal '''hubbub''' wild}}
#*: Of stunning sounds and voices all confused,
#*: Borne through the hollow dark, assaults his ear
#*: With loudest vehemence.

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:commotion]]

